# Map & UI performance

Client-side scale pressure is the WebGL map and its DOM markers, `pois.json` parse, and localStorage — not combat resolution.

## Store subscriptions

- **Do not** subscribe `GameScreen` (or any map parent) to the whole `combat` object — gauge ticks rewrite it at 20 Hz
- Select booleans/scalars only; let `CombatPanel` own combat state
- Do not add `log` or per-frame search progress to a slice the map subscribes to

## POI layers

- **Viewport-cull** POIs: bounds padded 0.2, cap 450 — never map every `locations` entry to a Marker/feature
- Hidden POIs must not become markers or GeoJSON features

## Code splitting

- Keep MapLibre out of the menu chunk — `React.lazy` for spawn/game/create/death screens
- Do not add a second mapping library

## State updates

- `advanceTime` / noise / faction expand must **preserve location identity** for untouched sites
- Cloning the whole `locations` record re-renders the map HUD — patch only changed ids

## Fog

- Fog is ground polygons (`src/map/fogGeometry.ts`): cached explored union minus the live disc
- Do not rebuild the explored union on energy ticks

## 3D buildings

- Drive the extrusion with feature-state only (rise, colour, selected) — never re-add or re-filter the layer per tick
- Overlays go through `installOverlay` slots, not raw `addLayer` with ad-hoc `beforeId`

## Example

```typescript
// BAD — re-renders map at 20 Hz
const combat = useGameStore((s) => s.combat);

// GOOD — scalar selectors
const inCombat = useGameStore((s) => s.combat !== null);
```
